From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] tour: Kiln OS's own tour of the AD5X screens

Upstream's first-run and "New in 1.1" tour points at tiles the AD5X
home doesn't have (nozzle_temps, printer_image), calls the IFS an AMS,
shows a Print Status sample with a quad gantry level step, and names an
"Advanced" panel with firmware updates. Printers that came from a Kiln
beta.18 image saw only its upgrade part ("New in 1.1", 1 / 5).

On HELIX_KILN_AD5X builds build_tour_steps() returns
build_kiln_tour_steps() (tour_steps_kiln.cpp): welcome to Kiln OS, the
top strip, the Print status tile, the IFS slots tile, customizing the
home screen, Controls, Load and unload, the IFS screen and its tools
(Auto-Refill, Tune IFS, Pre-feed), More (the dots button) and Settings
with Kiln's rows. The IFS steps only with a filament system. No Print
Status sample. Upstream's list stays as it is for other builds.

kTourVersion is 3 (kKilnTourVersion) on the AD5X build, so someone who
finished or skipped upstream's tour (1 or 2) sees Kiln's once, starting
with a "A tour of Kiln's screens" card instead of the welcome. Replay
Welcome Tour in Help & About shows the full Kiln tour. Strings in en
and ru.
